Adversarial Steganography Datasets
This directory contains the datasets used for training and evaluating the adversarial steganography and steganalysis models. 
Below are the standard benchmark datasets recommended for this project.

1. BOSSbase 1.01
Download Links: Kaggle Dataset | DDE Binghamton Database
Description: BOSSbase 1.01 is a commonly used benchmark dataset for steganography and steganalysis research. 
Originally created for the "Break Our Steganographic System" (BOSS) competition, it consists of 10,000 grayscale images. 
For many modern deep learning implementations, these images are often cropped or resized to 256x256 pixels.

2. BOWS-2 (Break Our Watermarking System 2)
Download Link: BOWS-2 Original Dataset (.tgz)
Description: Originally developed for an image watermarking competition, the BOWS-2 dataset is frequently utilized in the steganography domain. 
In steganalysis research, it is highly common to combine this dataset with BOSSbase to expand the available training data. 
This significantly helps prevent overfitting when training complex deep neural networks.
